.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUSTYFI_LIB_ROOT
Library root, when
.B \-\-lib\-root
is not given.
.TP
.B RUSTYFI_FONT_DIR
Font root, when
.B \-\-font\-dir
is not given.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base of the compile-cache directory.
.TP
.B RUSTYFI_OFFLINE
Make the package manager fail cleanly instead of reaching the network.
.TP
.B RUSTYFI_REGISTRY_TOKEN
Bearer token for registry tarball downloads over HTTP.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <lib\-root>/dist/packages/
SATySFi 0.0 packages.
.TP
.I <lib\-root>/dist\-v01/packages/
SATySFi 0.1 packages.
.TP
.I <lib\-root>/dist/fonts/
Bundled font files, each with its licence beside it.
.TP
.I <lib\-root>/dist/hash/fonts.rustyfi\-hash
Maps a font name used by a document to the file that provides it;
.I default\-font.rustyfi\-hash
names the regular, bold, oblique and math defaults.
.TP
.I <doc>.satysfi\-aux
Cross-reference table, in the same JSON format upstream SATySFi writes, so the
two interoperate.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success, non-zero if the document fails to load, typecheck, evaluate or
render, or if a package operation fails.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compile a document with the packages and fonts from an unpacked release:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ export RUSTYFI_LIB_ROOT=/opt/rustyfi/lib/rustyfi
$ rustyfi doc.saty \-o doc.pdf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Preview the same layout in a browser, and see where the time goes:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ rustyfi doc.saty \-\-format html
$ rustyfi doc.saty \-\-timing
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README and manual, and upstream SATySFi:
.UR https://github.com/gfngfn/SATySFi
.UE .
.SH LICENSE
LGPL-3.0. The bundled fonts keep their own licences, which travel beside them
in
.IR <lib\-root>/dist/fonts/ .
